  "evaluation": "All three correctly classify the disagreement as genuine and identify design_or_bias as primary: a cross-sectional vitamin D–status association versus a randomized supplementation trial. Neither finding is off-question, and neither provides grounds for calling the conflict apparent. B and C also capture the comparator difference (normal vitamin D status versus placebo), alongside population, intervention, and outcome-measure differences. B is slightly clearer and more concise than C; A is substantively correct but lists fewer secondary differences.",
